id: pm-gh1625
title: "GH-1625: align extension-refusal Sentry capture with declared contracts and telemetry source context"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1625 identifies handled pm-presets SimulationRefusal events from host2026.10.25 in production Sentry without telemetry source_context. Investigate the documented extension-refusal boundary and provenance propagation; distinguish authorized declared refusals from unexpected exceptions instead of suppressing every object with a code. Retain unknown/unhandled fault admission and verify the actual emitting host/package versions. This producer concern is separate from upstream SDK resolution and the release-blocker investigation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T14:47:48.858Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T00:16:33.270Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-29T23:35:29.681Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T23:35:29.681Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce through real extension host and classify only validated declared refusal contracts; Preserve capture of unknown codes mismatched contracts and unexpected or unhandled exceptions; Verify privacy-safe source_context host version and extension version propagation; Prove test isolation and fresh live telemetry without resolving historical faults solely to clear a gate
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: medium
resolution: Preserve separately bundled expected refusals; wrap unknown handler failures as unexpected runtime errors with local causes; share CLI/action/template failure construction; attach owner/version/source context without tracing and keep mutable SDK log/event context in the isolation scope.
expected_result: "Declared SDK refusals retain their contract, unexpected faults stay observable with actionable provenance, and Node/Bun CLI and embedded hosts honor source attribution, consent and diagnostic privacy."
actual_result: "Latest linked receipt test-local-mvu69wd6-3pipra passes 687 tests, with four TypeScript projects and focused ESLint passing. Actual Node/Bun loopback controls reproduced the prior capture, privacy and scope bugs; corrected collectors and clean installed packed-SDK probes pass, including sequential generic logs and exceptions."
